ider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.2,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":20.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"WaterBridge Infrastructure LLC, water infrastructure company, provides water management solutions through integrated pipeline and water handling networks in the United States. It offers produced water handling and gathering pipeline services; brackish water, recycled water, and produced water solutions; and gas transportation services. The company was incorporated in 2025 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jason  Long | CEO & Director | Age 43 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 540 people. Revenue per employee of $973K ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["WaterBridge Infrastructure LLC is a mid-cap energy business with a $3.1B market cap on $526M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $119M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 21.6% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 45% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 125% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 67% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6686667642324013},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $584.1M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-584136544.92},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Energy peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Energy peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"WaterBridge raises FY2026 adjusted EBITDA outlook to $465M-$485M while lowering capex midpoint (NYSE:WBI)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4667370-waterbridge-raises-fy2026-adjusted-ebitda-outlook-to-465m-485m-while-lowering-capex-midpoint","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793914653.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.153,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"WBI (NYSE:WBI) Issues Quarterly Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/wbi-nysewbi-issues-quarterly-earnings-results.html","date":"2